From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 19:51:20 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Dolby Vision: a restart for another output configures the
 renderer again

The video OSD's Output mode (kodi-9962) restarts the title with
TMSG_MEDIA_RESTART, and SelectOutputSettings applies the choice when
the restarted title is prepared, but the output never changed. The
restart reopens the title in the same VideoPlayer (PLAYER_OPENFILE):
the renderer stays configured, and CRenderManager::Configure leaves it
so while the pictures keep their size, colours and buffer format,
which they do when only the output changes. The window chooses its
output only when the renderer is configured: SetVideoOutput ends the
output it has, CLinuxRendererGLES::Configure latches whether the
pictures go through the bridge, BeginDVBridge begins the video's, and
an output already begun stays what it is. So the tunnel, the engine
and the signal kept the output the title started with.

The other restarts that change the output have the same fault: an
output refused while the title plays (ten refused HDR10 commits,
TunnelHDR10Presented; ten refused player-led commits,
TunnelLLDVPresented; the engine refusing player-led for the TV's
target, LLDVRefused), which should restart the title with the
Automatic fallback's output, and the engine not starting or refusing
the title's pictures (StartFailed, TitleRefused), which should restart
it as plain base-layer video. Each kept the refused output, with no
picture drawn.

All six now restart through DVBRIDGE::RestartForOutput. It marks the
restart; SelectOutputSettings turns the mark into a one-shot request
when the restarted title is prepared, and the render manager
configures the renderer again for that title's first picture: the old
output ends and the window begins the new one, as when a title starts.
HDR10 <-> HDR10+ of a Dolby Vision video still switches while it
plays, without a restart.

Restarts for anything else (Kodi's own, for an audio passthrough
change) are unchanged, and nothing changes when no output is refused
and the OSD list is not used: the request is set only for a title one
of these restarts reopened, and cleared each time a title is prepared.
